{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And when you reap.</b> In plural voice, for so the language of the parashah began; and moreover because it is the custom at harvest time that many reap together. And it says לא תכלה in singular voice, for it gives warning regarding the commandment of pe'ah and leket to the individual owner of the field, and likewise to the individual owner of the vineyard regarding the commandment of olelot and peret. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived: ״שדך״ — I have only 'your field'; if he had a field in partnership, from where do we know he is obligated in pe'ah? Scripture says: ״ובקצרכם את קציר ארצכם״ — 'and when you reap the harvest of your land.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:46.557737731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}